---
source: crates/rune-cli/tests/cli.rs
expression: surface
---
$ rune --help
Centralized script runner for JS/TS monorepos

Usage: rune <COMMAND>

Commands:
  run      Run a script by name
  list     List all available scripts
  inspect  Show how a script resolves and where it comes from
  init     Write a starter rune.config.ts in the current directory
  cache    Manage the resolved-config cache
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

$ rune run --help
Run a script by name

rune's own options come before the script name. Everything after the name is appended to the script's command, whether or not a `--` separates it.

Usage: rune run [OPTIONS] <NAME> [ARGS]...

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          The script to run

  [ARGS]...
          Arguments appended to the script's command

Options:
      --root
          Resolve against the root config only, ignoring this package's definitions

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

$ rune list --help
List all available scripts

Usage: rune list

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ rune inspect --help
Show how a script resolves and where it comes from

Usage: rune inspect [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>  The script to explain

Options:
      --root  Resolve against the root config only, ignoring this package's definitions
  -h, --help  Print help

$ rune init --help
Write a starter rune.config.ts in the current directory

Usage: rune init [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --from-package-json  Seed the starter with the scripts from the nearest package.json
  -h, --help               Print help

$ rune cache --help
Manage the resolved-config cache

Usage: rune cache <COMMAND>

Commands:
  clear  Remove every cached config result
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help

$ rune cache clear --help
Remove every cached config result

Usage: rune cache clear

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help
